# Quoting Engine Core Principles

This app is an **estimating and quoting engine**, not a transcript-to-preview renderer. Every change must preserve the full pipeline.

## A workflow is only working when ALL of these are aligned:
- Customer preview (correct title, scope, materials, optional works — no internal data)
- Internal review (labour quantities, materials, assumptions, warnings, flags)
- Pricing facts (line items with correct quantities and rates)
- Matched JMS lines (item codes, account codes, tax codes)
- Xero/JMS export (descriptions, quantities, prices, codes — all correct)

## Hours are quantities, never currency

`Allow 7 hours` → labour quantity of **7 h**, NOT a pricing fact of `$7`.

```
// ❌ BAD — treats "Allow 7 hours" as a $7 allowance
extractPricing("Allow 7 hours to remove edging") → { amount: 7 }

// ✅ GOOD — labour hour phrases are quantities, not prices
labourQuantity("Allow 7 hours to remove edging") → { hours: 7, task: "remove edging" }
```

Labour total for a multi-task job = **sum of all tasks**, not just the first.

## Optional works must stay separate

Optional works must never be merged into the main quote scope. They must appear in a distinct `Optional Works` section, both in customer preview and internal review.
